{"step_index":304,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:11:22Z","content":"Everything looks clean. Here's a summary of everything that was implemented across `index.html` and `app.js`:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Real-Time Orbit Propagation\n- Each satellite entity now uses a **`Cesium.SampledPositionProperty`** instead of a static `Cartesian3` position. I propagate each TLE across a full **24-hour window** (−12h to +12h) in **2-minute increments** using `satellite.js`, generating 720 position samples per object.\n- **Lagrange polynomial interpolation** (`interpolationDegree: 5`) smoothly fills in the gaps between samples. Cesium now automatically moves every satellite along its physically accurate orbit as the internal clock changes — whether via the scrubber, play button, or speed multiplier.\n- The `viewer.clock` is properly bounded with `startTime`, `stopTime`, and `CLAMPED` range to match the ±12 hour propagation window.\n\n### 2. Time Machine UI Upgrades\n- **► Play / ❚❚ Pause** toggle button that controls `viewer.clock.shouldAnimate`. The scrubber and time label auto-sync during playback via an `onTick` listener.\n- **Speed Multiplier** button group (1x, 10x, 60x, 100x) that sets `viewer.clock.multiplier`. Active button gets a highlighted style.\n- **⚠ JUMP TO TCA** button. Clicking any row in the Live Tracking table now registers that conjunction's approach time. When you switch to 3D and click this button, the clock instantly snaps to the exact millisecond of closest approach.\n\n### 3. Dynamic Collision Proximity Alerts\n- An `onTick` listener continuously computes the **real-time distance** between the two objects in the active conjunction using `Cesium.Cartesian3.distance()`.\n- When distance drops below **50 km**, a glowing red **`PolylineGlowMaterialProperty`** laser beam is drawn between the two satellites using a `CallbackProperty` (so it updates every frame). A pulsing **⚠ PROXIMITY ALERT — COLLISION IMMINENT ⚠** banner appears at the bottom of the 3D view.\n- When the objects drift apart again, the laser and alert are cleanly removed.\n\n**Please refresh your browser at http://localhost:3000**. Click any conjunction row to register it, switch to the 3D tab, hit ► Play at 60x speed, and watch the satellites physically move along their orbits. Use ⚠ JUMP TO TCA to snap to the moment of closest approach!"}
{"step_index":305,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:20:56Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"The 'Jump to TCA' button shows a crude browser alert: 'No conjunction selected. Click a row in Live Tracking first.' Let's make this feature bulletproof, functional, and cinematic.Please update app.js and index.html with the following:Smart Fallback (Never Show Alert):If no conjunction is currently selected when 'JUMP TO TCA' is clicked, do not trigger a browser alert. Instead, automatically default to the highest-risk conjunction (the CRITICAL event, e.g., COSMOS 2251 DEB vs STARLINK-1007).Precision Clock Jump:Parse the TCA timestamp into a Cesium.JulianDate.Set viewer.clock.currentTime = tcaJulianDate.Pause the clock (viewer.clock.shouldAnimate = false) so the user can inspect the exact closest approach moment.Update the timeline slider position and time label so they reflect the exact TCA time.Dual-Object Dynamic Framing:Instead of locking to just one object, calculate the midpoint between the two conjunction entities at TCA.Smoothly fly the camera (viewer.camera.flyTo) to a vantage point that frames both objects and their orbital trails, keeping the 4K Earth visible beneath them.Encounter Telemetry Overlay:Draw a pulsing red proximity line between the two objects.Open a floating glassmorphism card titled // CONJUNCTION ENCOUNTER (TCA) showing:Primary: Object 1 NameSecondary: Object 2 NameMiss Distance at TCA: e.g., 1.20 kmCollision Probability ($P_c$): e.g., 1.42e-4Relative Velocity: e.g., 14.2 km/sAdd a button [ Resume Simulation ] that unpauses the Cesium clock at 10x speed so the user can watch the objects fly past each other.Action: Update the code. Switch to the 3D Viewer tab without clicking the table, click 'JUMP TO TCA', and verify that the camera smoothly frames the encounter and displays the telemetry overlay. Take a screenshot.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T01:50:56+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
